    "body": "## Motivation\n\nRouted experts of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash are not used evenly. With expert parallelism, the most loaded EP rank sets the pace of every MoE layer. SGLang can already place experts at startup from recorded per-expert counts (`--expert-distribution-recorder-mode stat`, then `--init-expert-location <dump>`). The model's cookbook page doesn't mention it.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdds \"3.7 Static Expert Placement\" to the DeepSeek-V4.1 cookbook:\n- how to record the counts on real traffic and restart with them;\n- what the dump holds;\n- what redundant experts add on top.\n\nNo code changes.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nGB300, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, DP2 TP2 EP2 prefill server, ABBA, 4 runs of 900 s each.\n\n| | prefill throughput (tok/s per rank) |\n|---|---|\n| trivial placement | 80,876 / 80,858 |\n| `--init-expert-location` (counts from the same traffic) | 82,990 / 82,684 (+2.4%) |\n| `--init-expert-location` (counts from random token ids) | 80,762 (no gain) |\n\nKV cache capacity is unchanged without redundant experts.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #40104689547](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40104689547)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40104689549](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40104689549)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
