      "changes": 23,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fautoregressive%2FDeepSeek%2FDeepSeek-V4_1.mdx?ref=342bafc4e38efc9717d6d3bd59d8cdd0d8267bf2",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "docs/cookbook/autoregressive/DeepSeek/DeepSeek-V4_1.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -343,3 +343,26 @@ sglang serve \\\n ```\n \n Front the server with `sglang_router --policy cache_aware --dp-aware`, so a multi-turn session lands on the DP rank already holding its prefix.\n+\n+### 3.7 Static Expert Placement\n+\n+Requests do not spread evenly over the 384 routed experts. With expert parallelism, every MoE layer waits for the EP rank whose experts got the most tokens. `--init-expert-location` places the experts at startup from recorded per-expert token counts, so each rank carries a similar load. Placement happens once at load: no redundant experts, no extra memory, no rebalancing while serving.\n+\n+Record the counts on the traffic you serve, then restart with them:\n+\n+```bash\n+# 1. Serve with the recorder on and replay representative traffic.\n+SGLANG_EXPERT_DISTRIBUTION_RECORDER_DIR=/data/eplb \\\n+sglang serve <your args> --expert-distribution-recorder-mode stat\n+\n+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30000/start_expert_distribution_record\n+# ... about 10 minutes of real requests ...\n+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:30000/dump_expert_distribution_record\n+\n+# 2. Serve with the dumped counts.\n+sglang serve <your args> --init-expert-location /data/eplb/<dump>.pt\n+```\n+\n+- The dump holds per-layer, per-expert token counts (the last 1000 forward passes by default; `--expert-distribution-recorder-buffer-size -1` keeps every pass). The placement is computed at startup, so one dump serves any EP size.\n+- Record on real requests. On a GB300 DP2 TP2 EP2 prefill server, counts recorded from agentic coding traffic raised prefill throughput on that traffic by 2.4%. Counts recorded from random token ids gave no gain on it.\n+- `--ep-num-redundant-experts N` adds replicas of the hottest experts on top. On the same server's step benchmark, 16 replicas cut step time by a further 0.4% and shrank the KV cache pool by 20%.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/342bafc4e38efc9717d6d3bd59d8cdd0d8267bf2/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fautoregressive%2FDeepSeek%2FDeepSeek-V4_1.mdx",
